.SS "int libusb_get_device_string (\fBlibusb_device\fP * dev, enum \fBlibusb_device_string_type\fP string_type, char * data, int length)"

.PP
Retrieve a device string without needing to open the device\&. Since version v1\&.0\&.30 \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x0100010C

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdev\fP the target device 
.br
\fIstring_type\fP the string type to retrieve 
.br
\fIdata\fP the data buffer for the UTF-8 encoded string\&. 
.br
\fIlength\fP the size of the data buffer in bytes\&. USB string descriptors cannot be longer than LIBUSB_DEVICE_STRING_BYTES_MAX\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
a negative error code or the actual string length in bytes including the null terminator\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlibusb_get_string_descriptor()\fP 

.PP
\fBlibusb_get_string_descriptor_ascii()\fP
.RE
.PP
This function works when the device is still closed since it relies on the operating system to provide the string\&. The operating system normally reads and caches the common string descriptors during USB enumeration\&.

.PP
Since the USB string descriptor could be processed by the OS, this function returns a UTF-8 encoded string\&.

.PP
The string will be returned untranslated or in the default OS language when supported by the OS and USB device\&.

.PP
One way to call this function is using a buffer on the stack: 
.PP
.nf
char buffer[LIBUSB_DEVICE_STRING_BYTES_MAX];
int ret = libusb_get_device_string(dev, LIBUSB_DEVICE_STRING_SERIAL_NUMBER, buffer, sizeof(buffer));
if (ret < 0) {
    // handle error
}

.fi
.PP

.PP
This function is commonly used to get the serial number to allow for device selection before opening the selected device\&. 
.SS "int libusb_get_config_string (\fBlibusb_device\fP * dev, uint8_t config_value, char * data, int length)"

